/-!
# Words lifting the exact Peirce graph images

Explicit words in the published Eisenstein generators lift the two required
three-dimensional graph images. A third word evaluates to minus identity.
Every word is checked through intermediate six-dimensional integer matrices;
no group presentation or ATLAS family label is used as recognition.

Numerical source: John Bray, ATLAS 6L34G1-Ar6aB0, with the row convention of
`Block.MatrixData`. The consumer is Aschbacher, Sporadic Groups (1994), 49.5,
p.283. `source/generate.py` reproduces the certificates.
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section
